WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.675
Nothing shows a captain’s skill like the last fifty feet to the dock, with six passengers and a full marina watching.

2
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:12.000
Today is about why a boat moves the way she does at low speed.

3
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.600
Start with something most new captains never notice.

4
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.750
A propeller doesn’t only push the boat ahead.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.600
It also shoves the stern sideways.

6
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.775
That’s propeller walk.

7
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:25.850
Look at the diagram.

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:32.425
On a single-screw boat with a right-hand propeller, the stern kicks slightly to starboard going ahead.

9
00:00:32.675 --> 00:00:35.625
In reverse, it walks strongly to port.

10
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:37.650
So think it through.

11
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.425
You’re coming in to stop alongside, and you give her a burst of reverse.

12
00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.400
Which side would you rather have the dock on?

13
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.050
The port side.

14
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:54.050
That burst of reverse stops the boat and pulls your stern in toward the dock at the same time.

15
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.700
Find out which way your boat walks before you need to know.
